//BUG="the core library's private helper is_whitespace collides with a user function of that name"
//OUT="1 0"

// The user's file is compiled together with src/core/*.cpl as one program
// with one namespace. Everything the core library uses internally is hidden
// behind a leading underscore — `_Str_from_raw`, `_VecIter`, the `_def_…`
// macros — except one: `fn is_whitespace c` in src/core/io.cpl, a helper for
// the `read_*` functions that is not part of what the library offers.
//
// It has one untyped argument, which is the signature anyone would write for
// their own. Declaring one fails the compile with
//
//     Found two equivalent signatures for function is_whitespace
//       --> src/core/io.cpl:1:4
//
// an error that points into a file the user does not have, about a function
// they never called.
//
// The fix is to give the helper the same underscore the other internals
// have.

fn is_whitespace c
    ret c == ' ' || c == '_'

fn main
    out "{is_whitespace('_')} {is_whitespace('x')}"
